meta {
  name: Recommend
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/adx/recommend?timespan=M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timespan: M5
  ~ticker: AAPL
  ~tickers: AAPL,TSLA,NVDA
  ~period: 14
  ~threshold: 25
  ~rising: 3
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # ADX Recommendation — BUY / SELL / HOLD

  A simple, actionable verdict from the ADX / +DI / −DI reading on the latest
  COMPLETED bar. Read-only — it does NOT place orders.

  ## Symbol resolution
  - `?ticker=AAPL`            — verdict for one symbol (returns a single object).
  - `?tickers=AAPL,TSLA,NVDA` — verdict for each (returns a list).
  - Neither given            — screens the whole configured universe
    (`webull.trading.universe-path`).

  ## Query
  - `timespan`  — bar granularity (default M1). M1/M5/M15/M30/M60/M120/M240/D/W/M/Y.
  - `period` / `threshold` / `rising` — optional overrides of `webull.adx.*`.

  ## How the verdict is decided
  Based on direction (+DI vs −DI) and strength (ADX) on the latest completed bar:
  - **BUY**  — confirmed/emerging up-trend: STRONG_UP, bullish reversal
    (+DI crosses above −DI with ADX >= threshold), or up-trend waking up
    (ADX low but rising, +DI on top).
  - **SELL** — the bearish mirror of the above.
  - **HOLD** — weak lean (ADX < threshold), no trend (choppy), or not enough data.

  ## Response
  Single ticker:
    { ticker, action (BUY|SELL|HOLD), reason, close }

  Multiple / universe:
    { source (requested|universe), timespan, evaluated,
      counts: { buy, sell, hold },
      recommendations: [ { ticker, action, reason, close } ],  # BUY first, then SELL, then HOLD
      timestamp }

  ## Notes
  - The verdict uses the last COMPLETED bar (drops the in-progress bar) so it
    doesn't flicker mid-candle.
  - This is a trend-strength recommendation only — it is not wired to order flow
    and does not consider your positions, buying power, or spread.
}
